  "id": "aptitudetreatment-interaction",
  "term": "aptitude–treatment interaction",
  "definition": "Aptitude–treatment interaction is when the effect of a learning method depends on a learner’s characteristics or preferences, so the same treatment does not work equally well for everyone. In this packet, it refers to outcomes changing according to the match between text modality and the learner’s preferred modality.",
